  "notes": "'āsām' is taken to refer back to the plants (vīrudhaḥ) of unit 1. 'śrāntasadām iva' is obscure; it is rendered literally ('like (the place) of those sitting tired'). 'vedhasaḥ' = ordainers/wise ones/worshippers (uncertain). The end 'tat vedhaso na vā' is read as an either/or: they know it, or not. bhūta here = 'being' or 'what has come to be'.",
